# nx multi-source configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy these lines into ~/.env (or export them in your shell) to enable
# multiple model sources. nx auto-loads ~/.env at startup.
#
# Each source needs at minimum a BASE_URL. API_KEY and MODEL are optional:
#   - API_KEY defaults to "sk-noop" (local servers ignore it)
#   - MODEL left blank → auto-resolved from the server's /v1/models
#
# API_KEY supports $indirection: $some_key means "look up the env var
# (or ~/.env key) named some_key". Useful when the key already lives
# somewhere and you don't want to duplicate it.

# Comma-separated list of source names. The first is the default at startup.
NX_SOURCES=local,zai

# --- local: llama.cpp / vLLM on this machine ---------------------------
NX_SOURCE_LOCAL_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
NX_SOURCE_LOCAL_API_KEY=sk-noop
# MODEL omitted → auto-resolved from server

# --- zai: Z.ai remote endpoint -----------------------------------------
NX_SOURCE_ZAI_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4
NX_SOURCE_ZAI_API_KEY=***         # pulls "zai_test" from ~/.env
NX_SOURCE_ZAI_MODEL=glm-x-preview

# --- bubbles: LAN proxy with a stale /v1/models (illustrates the pin) ---
# NX_SOURCES=bubbles,local
# NX_SOURCE_BUBBLES_BASE_URL=http://172.29.180.65:4000/v1
# NX_SOURCE_BUBBLES_API_KEY=***
# NX_SOURCE_BUBBLES_MODEL=glm-5.3
# The proxy's GET /v1/models can keep retired ids listed (e.g. ones that
# 400 "Invalid model name") and lags on new ones. Pin the true
# lineup so the /source bubbles <model> dropdown matches what's actually
# served (comma-separated, whitespace-tolerant; embeddings-only ids like
# qwen3-embedding-8b are left out — /source switches chat models):
# NX_SOURCE_BUBBLES_MODELS=glm-5.3,glm-5.3-flash,qwen3.8-flash-next,qwen3.8-27b,deepseek-v4-pro

# --- together: built-in convenience source (Together AI) ---------------
# If TOGETHER_API_KEY is set (here or in your shell), nx auto-registers a
# `together` source at https://api.together.xyz/v1 defaulting to GLM-5.3.
# No NX_SOURCE_TOGETHER_* vars needed — just:
TOGETHER_API_KEY=***

# Together hosts many models, so /source takes an optional model override:
#   /source together                    # → zai-org/GLM-5.3 (the default)
#   /source together zai-org/GLM-4.6    # → any other Together model id
# It's registered last, so it never displaces your default startup source.
# Defining NX_SOURCE_TOGETHER_* below overrides the built-in entirely:
# NX_SOURCE_TOGETHER_BASE_URL=https://api.together.xyz/v1
# NX_SOURCE_TOGETHER_API_KEY=$TOGETHER_API_KEY
# NX_SOURCE_TOGETHER_MODEL=zai-org/GLM-5.3

# Override the starting source (optional — defaults to the first in NX_SOURCES)
# export NX_ACTIVE=zai

# --- split roles across servers (uses idle inference) ---------------------
# Any satellite call can ride a different server than the active one:
#   compression/context-fold, sub-agents, evidence reducer.
# Unset → each role uses the active source like everything else.
# NX_COMPRESS_SOURCE=bubbles   NX_COMPRESS_MODEL=deepseek-4.1-flash
# NX_SUBAGENT_SOURCE=bubbles   NX_SUBAGENT_MODEL=qwen3.8-flash-next
# NX_REDUCER_SOURCE=bubbles    NX_REDUCER_MODEL=glm-5.3-flash

# Unattended multi-phase campaigns: when a todo plan is mid-flight AND this
# session has spawned a write/implement/advisor agent, each finished agent's
# wake turn is told to review the result and spawn the next phase instead of
# wrapping up — so the plan advances while you are away. This caps how many
# consecutive auto-continuations may chain without a typed message (default
# 25; any typed turn, even a slash command, resets it). NX_WAKE_PROMPT=0
# still turns auto-continuation off entirely.
# NX_WAKE_STREAK_LIMIT=25

# Vision (opt-in like NX_NATIVE_TOOLS): offers the read_image tool once a
# source has confirmed native tool calls. png/jpeg/gif/webp/bmp; base64
# inflates 4/3x, so keep NX_IMAGE_MAX_BYTES modest on small local windows.
# NX_VISION=1
# NX_IMAGE_MAX_BYTES=1048576

# --- web_fetch: keyless web access (tier-1 always-on) --------------------
# GET-only fetches + DuckDuckGo-lite search, heavily cached and throttled.
# A self-hosted SearXNG is the PREFERRED search backend (exempt from the
# DDG throttle, your own instance): enable `formats: [html, json]` in its
# settings.yml and point NX_SEARX_URL at the instance root.
# NX_SEARX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888
# Optional Basic auth for limiter-on / authed instances ("user:pass"):
# NX_SEARX_AUTH=user:pass
# Max results rendered from the first page (default 10):
# NX_SEARX_MAX_RESULTS=10
# NX_WEBFETCH=0                 # remove the tool (fully offline hosts)
# NX_WEBFETCH_MAX_BYTES=20000   # readable-text cap per page
# NX_WEBFETCH_SEARCH_INTERVAL=3 # seconds between DDG-lite searches
# NX_WEBFETCH_HOST_INTERVAL=2   # seconds between fetches of the same host
# NX_WEBFETCH_CACHE_TTL=604800  # 7-day global cache (ETag-revalidated)
# NX_WEBFETCH_ROBOTS=0          # opt out of robots.txt (default on)
# NX_WEBFETCH_ALLOW_PRIVATE=0   # 1 lifts the SSRF guard on a trusted network

# Color theme (optional — mocha default). /theme switches live & saves here.
# Available: mocha / latte / dracula / nord / gruvbox / vaporwave / amethyst
# NX_THEME=dracula

# Waiting animation (optional — on by default). The calm 12-cell sweep bar
# changes at most two glyphs per frame. 0 disables animation entirely and
# shows a static status line instead (photosensitivity-friendly).
# NX_SPINNER=0

# Repin one semantic role to a palette hue or an exact hex, independent of the
# theme. <hue> is one of cyan/green/yellow/red/magenta/gray/blue/orange and
# tracks /theme; a 6-digit hex is theme-independent. See README "Themes".
# NX_ACCENT_COLOR=magenta
# NX_TOOL_OUTPUT_COLOR=#fdfd96

# Live sub-agent surface (EVENTSURFACE_SPEC: /tabs, Ctrl-T). Display-only:
# nothing here enters the transcript or reaches the model.
# NX_EVENT_TAIL_LINES=200  # ring lines kept per background agent in the sink
# NX_TABS_HEIGHT=8         # max rows of the live region (clamped 1..20)

# --- telegram: personal gateway (nx telegram) ---------------------------
# Drive nx from a chat: paper links, uploaded PDFs, plain instructions.
# Token from @BotFather; chat ID from messaging the bot once and reading
# `getUpdates` (or @userinfobot). The allowlist is HARD: empty = refuse to
# start. Gated calls (writes, shell) auto-deny unless you launch `nx
# telegram --yolo` — for ingestion-only use, leave the default posture.
# NX_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABC-your-token
# NX_TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHATS=123456789
# NX_TELEGRAM_POLL_INTERVAL=1.0
